{
  "$comment": "Which recorded tracks feed each firearm sound of assets/sfx-inbox/armas. `ffl` is The Free Firearm Sound Library (Ben Jaszczak, Kickstarter 2014, CC0; mirror github.com/buddingmonkey/FreeFirearmsSFXLibrary, track codes of its Master Sheet.xlsx). `rfs` is the Restrained Firearms Soundpack (envalid.com, CC BY 4.0; github.com/sakkaku/restrained-firearms-soundpack). Each track holds several repetitions of the action: cut.mjs splits them into takes. Shots: `close` = the near microphone, `far` = the mid-distance one. Reload cues end in `_light` (pistols, revolvers), `_medium` (rifles, bolt and lever guns) or `_heavy` (shotguns): the strength tiers game-audio picks by the weapon's weight. `oap` is the Oculus Audio Pack 1 (Oculus sound design team, 2015, CC BY 4.0; github.com/facebookincubator/Meta-open-sound, corpora/oculus-audio-pack/ogg): whole files, one take each. Casings: a case's bounces on one floor (`casing_drop_<concreto|terra|metal>`), played on the first hit.",
